# Portfolio · Project Overview

**Stack**: Next.js 16 (App Router, Turbopack) · React 19 · TypeScript 5.9 · Tailwind v4 (CSS-only config) · shadcn/ui `new-york` · `motion/react` for animation.

**Package manager**: `npm` only. Lockfile is `package-lock.json`. Do not introduce `yarn.lock`, `pnpm-lock.yaml`, or `bun.lock`.

## Layout

- `src/app/` — App Router. RSCs by default. Route groups under `(root)`.
- `src/components/ui/` — shadcn primitives. Treat as **vendored**; keep diffs minimal.
- `src/components/sections/` — page-level composed sections.
- `src/components/*.tsx` — app-specific shared components.
- `src/lib/utils.ts` — `cn()` lives here. Always use it for conditional classes.
- `src/app/globals.css` — Tailwind v4 + design tokens. **There is no `tailwind.config.ts`.**

## Always after substantive changes

```bash
npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run build
```

If any of these fail, fix them before declaring the task done.

## Hard "don'ts"

- ❌ `import { motion } from "framer-motion"` → use `"motion/react"`.
- ❌ Adding a `tailwind.config.ts` — Tailwind v4 is configured via CSS in `globals.css`.
- ❌ Bumping `zod` to v4 without an explicit migration plan.
- ❌ Bumping `lucide-react` to `1.x` (brand icons removed; would break `src/data/links.ts`).
- ❌ Bumping `eslint` to `10.x` (incompatible with `eslint-plugin-react` shipped by `eslint-config-next`).
- ❌ Using `next lint` — it was removed in Next 16. Use `eslint .`.
